<title>NEW ZEALAND: New Zealand yields close little changed.</title>
<headline>New Zealand yields close little changed.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>---------------Snapshot at close-----------------</p>
<p>Figures in brackets compare against previous day's close</p>
<p>FUTURES					  PHYSICAL YIELD</p>
<p>90-DAY BILLS (MAR) 92.68  (+0.03)	90-DAYS 7.88   (-0.02)</p>
<p>3-YR BONDS   (MAR) 92.99 (PREV 92.98)  02/00   7.04   (-0.01)</p>
<p>10-YR BONDS  (MAR) 92.70 (PREV 92.69)  11/06   7.30   (-0.01)</p>
<p>OVERNIGHT CASH 7.90 PCT (PREV 7.95)    US 5-YR  6.15 (PREV 6.12)</p>
<p>NZD/USD 0.7072/79 (PREV 0.7069/76)     US 10-YR 6.36 (PREV 6.35)</p>
<p>TWI 67.40 (PREV 67.43)		     US 30-YR 6.60 (PREV 6.60)</p>
<p>--------------------------(Dec 23)------------------------------</p>
<p>* Yields end little changed</p>
<p>* Market already on holiday</p>
<p>* No change expected</p>
<p>New Zealand yields closed virtually unchanged on Monday in a market that showed no inclination to go anywhere.</p>
<p>Dealers said there was passing interest in a $200 million eurokiwi by the World Bank announced on Friday and some mild buying on the back of it.</p>
<p>But the 370 volume in the bank bill futures market told the story -- there was no real interest and Tuesday is likely to be similar.  </p>
